'''Alluri Sitharama Raju district''', also known as '''Alluri district'''<ref>{{Cite web |title=Andhra Pradesh government may bifurcate newly-formed Alluri Sitarama Raju district |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2022/apr/06/andhra-pradeshgovernmentmay-bifurcate-newly-formed-alluri-sitarama-raju-district-2438567.html |access-date=2022-07-09 |website=The New Indian Express}}</ref> and by its initials as '''ASR district''',<ref>{{Cite news |date=2 June 2022 |title=Coastal Andhra Pradesh to witness intense heatwave during next three days; mercury may touch 47°C |language=en-IN |work=[[The Hindu]] |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/coastal-andhra-pradesh-to-witness-intense-heatwave-during-next-three-days-mercury-may-touch-47c/article65488135.ece |access-date=3 June 2022 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref> is a district in the Indian state of [[Andhra Pradesh]]. The headquarters of the district is located at [[Paderu]]. Named after [[Alluri Sitarama Raju]], a revolutionary in the [[Indian independence movement]] who hailed from the region. The district is known for its scenery and lies in the [[Eastern Ghats]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Apparasu |first=Srinivasa Rao |date=3 January 2023 |title=Andhra Pradesh: Hamlet nestled in Eastern Ghats a popular winter getaway |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/andhra-pradesh-hamlet-nestled-in-eastern-ghats-a-popular-winter-getaway-101672685841015.html |access-date=26 September 2024 |website=Hindustan Times}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Gopal |first=B. Madhu |date=17 October 2022 |title=Andhra Pradesh: As winter nears, Lambasingi beckons tourists |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/as-winter-nears-lambasingi-beckons-tourists/article66022076.ece |access-date=26 September 2024 |work=The Hindu |language= |issn=0971-751X}}</ref>

==Etymology==
[[File:Alluri Sita Rama Raju statue.jpg|thumb|A statue of [[Alluri Sitarama Raju]]|left]]

This district is named after [[Alluri Sitarama Raju]], a revolutionary in the Indian independence movement who came from the region.<ref>{{Cite news |last= |first= |date=8 August 2021 |title=Call to draw inspiration from Alluri |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/call-to-draw-inspiration-from-alluri/article35806018.ece |access-date=26 September 2024 |work=The Hindu |language= |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Rao |first=G. Janardhana |date=4 April 2022 |title=Andhra district named after Alluri, his memorials in neglect |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2022/Apr/04/andhra-district-named-after-alluri-his-memorials-in-neglect-2437679.html |access-date=26 September 2024 |website=The New Indian Express |language=}}</ref>

== History ==
In July 2019, on the occasion of Alluri Sitarama Raju's 122nd birth anniversary, state Tourism Minister [[Muttamsetti Srinivasa Rao|Avanthi Srinivasa Rao]] said a newly formed district would be named after Alluri Sitarama Raju.<ref name="nee1">{{cite web |date=5 July 2019 |title=New district will be named after Alluri: Minister |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2019/jul/05/new-district-will-be-named-after-alluri-minister-1999664.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191028054433/http://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2019/jul/05/new-district-will-be-named-after-alluri-minister-1999664.html |archive-date=28 October 2019 |access-date=26 January 2022 |website=[[The New Indian Express]]}}</ref>
The district was proposed on 26 January 2022 by the [[Y. S. Jagan Mohan Reddy]]'s government as part of a reorganisation of all the existing 13 districts in the state to form 26 districts in total. Final notification was issued by the [[Government of Andhra Pradesh]] on 3 April 2022 and the district was effective from 4 April 2022. The administrative headquarters of the district is located at [[Paderu]]. It was formed from [[Paderu revenue division]] of [[Visakhapatnam district]] and [[Rampachodavaram revenue division]] of [[East Godavari district]].<ref>{{Cite news|last=Raghavendra|first=V.|date=26 January 2022|title=With creation of 13 new districts, AP now has 26 districts|work=[[The Hindu]]|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/with-creation-of-13-new-districts-ap-now-has-26-districts/article38327788.ece|url-status=live|access-date=26 January 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220126110443/https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/with-creation-of-13-new-districts-ap-now-has-26-districts/article38327788.ece|archive-date=26 January 2022|issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=30 March 2022|title=New districts to come into force on April 4|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/new-districts-to-come-into-force-on-april-4/article65274658.ece|access-date=31 March 2022|website=[[The Hindu]]|language=en}}</ref>

On December 31st 2025, Rampachodavaram division was carved out of this district and formed as a new district named '''[[Polavaram district]]'''.<ref>{{cite web |title=Andhra Pradesh Cabinet approves formation of two new districts, headquarters status for Madanapalle|url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2025/Dec/30/andhra-pradesh-cabinet-approves-formation-of-two-new-districts-headquarters-status-for-madanapalle |date=30 December 2025 |website=[[The New Indian Express]] |language=en }}</ref>

==Geography==
The district is bordered to the north by [[Malkangiri district]] and [[Koraput district]] in [[Odisha]], to the west by [[Polavaram district]], to the south by [[Anakapalli district]], and to the east by [[Vizianagaram district]] and [[Parvathipuram Manyam district]]s.{{citation needed|date= September 2022}}

== Administrative divisions ==
The district has one revenue division, namely [[Paderu revenue division|Paderu]], which is further subdivided into a total of 11 mandals, each administered by a Tahsildar.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=కొత్త జిల్లా తాజా స్వరూపం |url=https://www.eenadu.net/telugu-news/ap-top-news/general/2501/122062849 |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=[[Eenadu.net]] |language=te}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Jonathan |first=P. Samuel |date=2022-09-07 |title=Andhra Pradesh: Cabinet clears investment proposals worth ₹1.25 lakh crore |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/andhra-pradesh-cabinet-clears-investment-proposals-worth-125-lakh-crore/article65862971.ece |access-date=2022-09-13 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=AP Issues GO Creating Polavaram District With Rampachodavaram as Headquarters
|url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/southern-states/andhra-pradesh/ap-issues-go-creating-polavaram-district-with-rampachodavaram-as-headquarters-1927331|date=30 December 2025 |website=[[Deccan Chronicle]] |language=en }}</ref>

